    "module": {
      "purpose": "Defines the foundational record types and runtime type guard used by the store package to identify records and enforce record-specific identifier typing.",
      "summary": "This module establishes the structural contract for store records: each record has a readonly identifier and type name, while branded identifiers prevent accidental mixing between record types at compile time. It also provides utility type extraction and a runtime predicate for validating unknown values before they are treated as records. The implementation is entirely type-level except for the small synchronous guard.",
      "businessContext": "Supports typed persistence and retrieval of heterogeneous domain records. If these contracts or validation rules fail, records may be misclassified or identifiers from different domains may be mixed unsafely.",
